From e8f56ae723cfab498e1d43c9ab8aafab0d39dc17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 07:44:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dhcpd: ipv4 = "static" in /etc/net/config.toml sets a fixed
 address (#622)

A section with ipv4 = "static" gives the interface the address from
address = "a.b.c.d/len" as soon as it appears, and keeps it when the link
goes down. router and the first of dns are optional; dhcpd treats the
fixed address like a lease that never ends, so it gets the default route
and the name server under the same rules as a DHCP lease (the first wired
interface wins). A missing or malformed value gives one line and skips
the section.
---
 dhcpd/src/main.rs | 173 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 143 insertions(+), 30 deletions(-)

